        "240",
        "GFCI",
        "plug|receptacle",
        "extension",
        "do not|keep.*off|confirm|verify"
      ],
      "run": {
        "answer": "Do not use an extension cord with this welder. The manual prohibits extension cords.\n\nSources: files/owner-manual.pdf p.20; files/owner-manual.pdf p.6; files/owner-manual.pdf p.7\n\nYour garage receptacle meets published basic electrical requirements: 240 VAC is a supported input option, the source is properly grounded, and GFCI protection is present.\n\nSources: files/owner-manual.pdf p.20; files/owner-manual.pdf p.6; files/owner-manual.pdf p.7\n\nYou cannot confirm safe direct connection because the assessment did not obtain information on specifications the manual requires: whether the source frequency is 60 Hz, whether delayed-action protection is present, the specific receptacle configuration, and the power cord type.\n\nSources: files/owner-manual.pdf p.20; files/owner-manual.pdf p.6; files/owner-manual.pdf p.7\n\nThe overall assessment result is incompatible. Before connecting to your receptacle, verify these missing specifications with your receptacle documentation or consult an electrician.\n\nSources: files/owner-manual.pdf p.20; files/owner-manual.pdf p.6; files/owner-manual.pdf p.7",
        "tools": [
          "assess_power_source"
        ],
